## Codegen
To regenerate every generated client in this repo, run:

```bash
task codegen
```

That covers both sides of the app and all schema sources, refreshing the openapi.json snapshot before any client is generated from it. Run `task --list` for the individual tasks if you only need one of them. This is the only sanctioned way to update generated code: nothing under a `generated/` folder should ever be hand-edited.{% endraw %}{% if has_backend %}{% raw %}

The Kiota clients of the backend (`frontend/app/generated/open-api/backend/` and `backend/tests/e2e/generated/open_api/backend/`) are not committed: they are build outputs of the committed OpenAPI snapshot.

- `task gen-openapi-clients` brings them up to date, and does nothing when they already are. Git hooks run it before each commit and after checkouts, merges and rebases, and a new devcontainer runs it once when it is created. Creating a git worktree fires no hook, so run it yourself in a new worktree.
- After changing the API, `task gen-openapi-snapshot` refreshes the snapshot and then the clients. Updating the snapshot with a bare `pytest --snapshot-update` leaves the clients stale until the next hook or task run.
- CI generates the clients in one job and hands them to the jobs that need them{% endraw %}{% if not deploy_as_executable %}{% raw %}, and the frontend image generates its own copy while it builds{% endraw %}{% endif %}{% raw %}.

Clients of other services, generated from something other than a committed file, are still committed.{% endraw %}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% raw %}

